1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:02,183
This code looks for 7 in a list.

2
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:07,233
Early Swift put backticks around the in that tells us where to look.

3
00:00:08,192 --> 00:00:10,575
In a loop, in is part of the grammar.

4
00:00:11,092 --> 00:00:15,658
In a call, the colon after it identifies it as a label.

5
00:00:16,175 --> 00:00:21,492
Swift 2.2, released in March 2016, allowed the backticks to be omitted here.

6
00:00:22,450 --> 00:00:24,442
The call with backticks still works.

7
00:00:24,958 --> 00:00:29,375
Both calls find the same 7 in the same list. Both return 1.
